TWEAK_NAME="Enable SSH"
TWEAK_RISK="medium"
TWEAK_EXPERIMENTAL=1
TWEAK_DESCRIPTION="Installs the public key in /data/opencmu/ssh/authorized_keys and prepends a key-only block to /etc/ssh/sshd_config. Requires OPENCMU_SSH_PUBKEY with one RSA key; OpenSSH 5.9 cannot use ed25519. Password logins are disabled, port 22 is enabled, and sshd is started on the live root unless OPENCMU_SSH_START=0. Rollback restores the config and removes the key file but does not stop an sshd that is already running."
